Description: Build sensord via PROG_EXTRA in debian/rules, and add the
 build-dependency it needs
 lm-sensors' upstream build only compiles the sensord program when
 PROG_EXTRA names it. Patch 0001 already adds the sensord binary package
 to debian/control, so without this the build "succeeds" but the sensord
 binary package ships with no /usr/sbin/sensord in it.
 .
 This used to be an environment variable on the dpkg-buildpackage command
 line in src/lm-sensors/Makefile, which only reached the local self-build.
 A Launchpad builder only ever sees the source package, so moving it into
 debian/rules makes it apply to the local build and PPA builds alike.
 .
 sensord also links against librrd (prog/sensord/Module.mk: -lrrd), which
 stock lm-sensors never declared as a build-dependency because it never
 actually built sensord. Add librrd-dev so the build environment has
 rrd.h and librrd available.
Origin: vendor
Forwarded: no
Author: Sheldon Qi <sheldon.qi@canonical.com>
Last-Update: 2026-07-29
--- a/debian/rules	2026-07-29 03:29:09.326375437 +0000
+++ b/debian/rules	2026-07-29 03:29:09.346907510 +0000
@@ -3,6 +3,12 @@
 export DEB_BUILD_MAINT_OPTIONS = hardening=+all
 export deb_systemdsleepdir = $(shell pkg-config --variable=systemdsleepdir systemd)
 
+# SONiC: lm-sensors' upstream build only compiles sensord when PROG_EXTRA
+# names it. The sensord binary package is added by patch 0001, but without
+# this the program itself is never built. This used to be an environment
+# variable in src/lm-sensors/Makefile, which a Launchpad builder cannot see.
+export PROG_EXTRA = sensord
+
 %:
 	dh $@
 
--- a/debian/control	2026-07-29 03:29:09.327597710 +0000
+++ b/debian/control	2026-07-29 03:29:09.368118378 +0000
@@ -4,6 +4,7 @@
 Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13),
                bison,
                flex,
+               librrd-dev,
                libtest-cmd-perl <!nocheck>,
                pkgconf,
                systemd-dev
